-r requirements.in
pytest==9.1.1
pytest-django==4.14.0
# Test-only: PDF text extraction for policy/tests/test_pdf_rendering.py's
# review-warnings assertions (M006-AUDIT-0004 finding I1) - reportlab's
# own content-stream layout splits a rendered run into multiple `Tj`
# fragments at markup-token boundaries (confirmed directly against this
# exact reportlab==5.0.1 by rendering escaped `<script>...</script>`-shaped
# text and inspecting the raw stream bytes), so a raw pdf_bytes substring
# check is not reliable for asserting rendered text content - pypdf's
# `extract_text()` correctly reconstructs the full run.
pypdf==6.19.0
# Test-only: real-browser (Chromium) acceptance testing (PID §16/§19/§28 -
# real-browser drawer/keyboard/XSS-execution proof, WI6 browser acceptance).
# Python package only - the Chromium browser binary itself is deliberately
# NEVER installed as part of any image build (this codebase's single
# Dockerfile is shared by both the dev/CI image and the exact-SHA release
# image - Central Architecture's "avoid introducing browser/runtime
# dependencies into the production application image unless genuinely
# required" instruction). `playwright install --with-deps chromium` is a
# runtime-only step, run against an already-built container's writable
# layer (see docs/runbooks/BROWSER-ACCEPTANCE-CAPABILITY.md), never part of
# this pinned, hash-locked dependency graph or any `RUN` line in the
# Dockerfile. Every existing `*_narrow_viewport_regression.py` /
# `test_responsive_text_regression.py` / `test_badge_narrow_viewport_
# regression.py` test already gates on `pytest.importorskip("playwright")`
# and is SKIPPED wherever this package is absent - installing it here is
# what turns those tests from skipped to genuinely running, everywhere this
# lock file is installed (dev image, CI).
playwright==1.63.0
